Market Overview
Butadiene, also known as 1,3-butadiene, is a key petrochemical feedstock used to manufacture synthetic rubber and several industrial polymers. It is primarily produced as a by-product of steam cracking and supports the production of styrene-butadiene rubber (SBR), butadiene rubber (BR), acrylonitrile-butadiene-styrene (ABS), and other downstream materials.

The material is particularly important to tire manufacturing, where synthetic rubber contributes to durability, traction, abrasion resistance, and rolling performance. It is also used in automotive components, construction materials, consumer goods, and specialty polymer applications.

Despite these established uses, the market faces pressure from volatile raw-material prices, changes in petrochemical production economics, and increasing sustainability requirements. Producers are evaluating operational improvements and alternative feedstocks to manage costs and respond to changing customer expectations.

